<title>USA: Tourism contributes $4.4 bln a year to Mississippi.</title>
<headline>Tourism contributes $4.4 bln a year to Mississippi.</headline>
<dateline>TUPELO, Miss. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tourism pumps $4.4 billion annually into Mississippi's economy, the Tupelo Daily Journal said Monday.</p>
<p>Tourism is the state's third-biggest industry, behind agriculture and health care. Without gaming, the figure drops to $2.26 billion a year.</p>
<p>The data were released state Department of Economic and Community Devlopment to coincide with this week's observation of National Tourism Week.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
